-- title:
--   Faithful Hecke lattice with Eichler–Shimura relation inside J_H[pⁿ]
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with finite residue field $k$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho\colon\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\operatorname{End}_k V$ trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and assume $\bar\rho$ becomes irreducible over $\overline k$. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N\neq 0$, let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$ prime, $q\notin S$) to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (lying in the decomposition group and acting on the residue field by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$), the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct nonzero naturals, each prime, outside $S$ and distinct from $r$, with homomorphisms $\pi_i\colon(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ (multiplicatively written) and scalars $\alpha_i\in k$; put $L=N(\prod_i q_i)r$ and $H=H_Q$ the intersection of $H_r$ with the kernel of the map built from the $\pi_i$. Assume the two commutation hypotheses `OpComm` and `DiaComm` (the operators $\mathrm{op}$ at level $L$ commute with each other, and the diamond operators commute with them), and assume $p\nmid L$. Write $\mathbb T$ for `HeckeRing`, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O}(ML)$ generated by the designated Hecke generators attached to these data. Then there exist $b\in\mathbb N$ and a monoid homomorphism $\delta\colon\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ such that: $\delta$ is trivial on the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $p$ as a nonunit; $\delta$ is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and there exist an abelian group $Y$ carrying compatible $\mathbb T$- and $\mathcal O$-module structures (with $\mathcal O$ acting through $\mathbb T$), finite and torsion-free over $\mathcal O$, a monoid homomorphism $\rho_Y\colon\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb T}(Y)$ and a monoid homomorphism $D\colon(\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb T}(Y)$, with the following properties. (i) $\mathbb T$ acts faithfully: $x\cdot y=0$ for all $y\in Y$ forces $x=0$. (ii) Each $D(u)$ commutes with each $\rho_Y(\sigma)$. (iii) For every $n$ there is a finite extension $F$ of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $F$ pointwise satisfies $\rho_Y(\sigma)y-y\in (p)^n Y$ for all $y$. (iv) Eichler–Shimura: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and $\ell\neq p$, every valuation subring $P$ with $\ell$ a nonunit and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, one has $\rho_Y(\sigma)^2-T_\ell\,\rho_Y(\sigma)+\ell\,D(\ell\bmod L)=0$ in $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb T}(Y)$, where $T_\ell\in\mathbb T$ is the corresponding Hecke operator. (v) For every $n$, writing $J=\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $L$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones) and $J[p^n]$ for its $p^n$-torsion, there is a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{star}$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to the additive automorphisms of $J[p^n]^b$ acting coordinatewise by $x\mapsto \langle\delta(\sigma)\rangle(\sigma\cdot x)$, and an additive map $\iota\colon Y\to J[p^n]^b$ with kernel exactly $(p)^nY$ satisfying $\iota(\rho_Y(\sigma)y)=\mathrm{star}(\sigma)(\iota y)$.
--
--   This is the geometric realisation step at Taylor–Wiles auxiliary level: the localised Hecke ring at level $L=N q_1\cdots q_t r$ acts faithfully on a lattice $Y$ carrying a Galois action that satisfies the Eichler–Shimura relation, and whose finite layers $Y/p^nY$ embed Galois-equivariantly, up to a diamond twist by a character $\delta$ unramified at $p$ and of finite level, into $b$ copies of the $p^n$-torsion of the Jacobian of $X_H$. It is the input to the statement producing surjectivity onto the level quotients of that torsion, where the twist being of finite level and unramified at $p$ is what permits the finite flatness argument.
